[32m+[m[32m### MenuProvider specificity rule[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use `MenuProvider_TodayMenu` only for broad requests such as "tell me today's menu" when no specific place and no specific meal-time are present.[m
[32m+[m[32m- If the command explicitly includes date/day, place, and meal-time, use `MenuProvider_GetMenu("<date> <place> <meal>")`.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Example: "오늘의 301동 점심 메뉴를 스피커로 알려줘." -> `menu = (#MenuProvider).menuprovider_getmenu("오늘 301동식당 점심")`[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Then speak the returned variable: `(#Speaker).speaker_speak(menu)`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Schedule and period policy[m
[32m+[m[32m- Encode wall-clock start times and day filters in `cron`, not by adding duplicate weekday/hour checks around the whole code.[m
[32m+[m[32m- If a command says "from X to Y every N minutes", set `cron` to the start time, set `period` to N minutes in milliseconds, and keep only the stop boundary in code. Example: from 10 PM to midnight every 10 minutes -> `cron: "0 22 * * *"`, `period: 600000`, code starts with `if ((#Clock).clock_hour == 0) { break }`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- For "from now until 3 PM" / "오후 3시까지", use the exact boundary guard `if ((#Clock).clock_hour == 15) { break }`, not `>= 15`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- If a command says "from now until midnight every N minutes", keep `cron: ""`, set `period`, and stop with `if ((#Clock).clock_hour == 0) { break }`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- If a command says "weekend afternoons every N minutes", encode weekend/start in cron such as `0 12 * * 6,7`, set `period`, and use code only for the end boundary.[m
[32m+[m[32m- If a command has two wall-clock actions in one scenario, use the first time as `cron` and a blocking `delay(...)` for the later action. Example: "8 AM odd blinds, 9 AM even blinds" -> `cron: "0 8 * * *"`, then `delay(1 HOUR)`, not `wait until clock_hour == 9`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Example: "Every 7 PM, if no one is detected on the 1st floor, turn off all lights; for the 2nd floor, check at 8 PM and turn off all its lights if no one is present." -> `cron: "0 19 * * *"`, `period: 0`, first check `#Floor1`, then `delay(1 HOUR)`, then check `#Floor2`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- For weekend periodic checks, encode the weekend window in cron such as `0 0 * * 6-7`, keep the explicit period, and keep a weekday guard if the GT policy requires it.[m
[32m+[m[32m- If a command has `cron`, set `period` to `0` unless there is an explicit repeated interval.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Trigger-then-repeat skeleton[m
[32m+[m[32m- For commands like "when/once X happens, then every N seconds/minutes do Y", set `period` to N milliseconds and use this skeleton:[m
[32m+[m[32m  ```[m
[32m+[m[32m  active := 0[m
[32m+[m[32m  if (active == 0) {[m
[32m+[m[32m      wait until (<trigger condition>)[m
[32m+[m[32m      active = 1[m
[32m+[m[32m  }[m
[32m+[m[32m  <repeated action>[m
[32m+[m[32m  ```[m
[32m+[m[32m- Do not put the repeated action only in an `else` branch. Do not reset the trigger flag unless the command explicitly says to stop when the trigger becomes false.[m
[32m+[m[32m- If there is a one-time immediate announcement before a later repeated action, keep the one-time announcement inside the `active == 0` block before `active = 1`, and put only the repeated action outside.[m
[32m+[m[32m- For smoke-triggered sirens in this dataset, use `siren_setsirenmode("fire")` for fire/smoke alarms, not `"emergency"`, unless the command explicitly says emergency.[m
[32m+[m[32m- For "drying is finished" on `LaundryDryer`, use `laundrydryer_spinspeed == 0`; do not invent `laundrydryer_dehumidifiermode`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- For repeating open/close window actions, use `windowcovering_uporopen()` and `windowcovering_downorclose()` with a state variable; do not use `window_open()` or `window_close()`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- For "whenever X is opened/locked" edge triggers, use `prev := ...`, `curr = ...`, and `if (prev != target and curr == target) { ... }`, then `prev = curr`; do not use a timer flag when the command asks for an edge event.[m
[32m+[m[32m- For midnight-to-6AM repeated light checks after closing the door, close the door once inside `active := 0`, then use `clock_hour == 6` as the stop guard and `lightsensor_brightness` for the brightness condition.[m
[32m+[m[32m- If a required slot is missing, do not invent it. Use the best generic value service from the injected service list.[m
