[32m+[m[32m  - Use the following condition at the start of your code block to stop execution on weekdays:[m
[32m+[m[32m### ✅ Required Behavior[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m- **Always insert a `break` statement when the repetition condition is no longer valid.**[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m- For scenarios that should only run on specific days (e.g., weekends), include logic such as:[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m'cron': '0 0 * * 0,6',[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m'period': 5000[m
[32m+[m[32m'code':[m
[32m+[m[32mweekday = (#Clock).clock_weekday[m
[32m+[m[32mif ((weekday != 'saturday') and (weekday != 'sunday')) {[m
[32m+[m[32m    break[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## period[m
[32m+[m[32m- `period` (Integer): Controls execution loop after cron trigger[m
[32m+[m[32m  - `-1`: Execute once, then stop.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - `0`: Execute once per cron trigger. (no further execution within the same cron cycle)[m
[32m+[m[32m  - `>= 100`: Repeat every period milliseconds (continuous monitoring).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## *break*: Stops current/future periods until next cron.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - **If the user command includes instructions to stop or terminate the repetition (for example, "반복을 중단해", "더 이상 반복하지 마", "중단", "until stopped", etc.), you must ensure the periodic execution loop is interrupted by using `break` inside the code block at the appropriate condition.**[m
[32m+[m[32m  - With cron = "": stops permanently after break[m
[32m+[m[32m  - With scheduled cron: stops until next cron trigger[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### [Example][m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mcode:[m
[32m+[m[32m  <flag> := true[m
[32m+[m[32m  if (<stop_condition>) {[m
[32m+[m[32m    break[m
[32m+[m[32m  }[m
[32m+[m[32m  if (<flag> == true) {[m
[32m+[m[32m    (#Tag).<action>()[m
[32m+[m[32m    <flag> = false[m
[32m+[m[32m  }[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## When to Use `period` over `cron`[m
[32m+[m[32m- If the user command includes "매초마다", "매 5분마다", "15초마다" 등 반복 주기 표현이 포함된 경우, You must always control repeated intervals **using period first**, not cron.[m
[32m+[m[32m  **반드시 `cron`이 아닌 `period`로 주기 반복을 제어해야 합니다.**[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Never use `while` in code**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Periodic Execution within Time Range in cron scenario[m
[32m+[m[32mTo run a scenario repeatedly **only within a specific hour range** (e.g., between 18:00 and 19:00), use `(#Clock).clock_hour` to conditionally check current time.[m
[32m+[m[32m### [Example][m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m{[m
[32m+[m[32mname : "Scenario1"[m
[32m+[m[32mcron : "<start hour cron>"[m
[32m+[m[32mperiod : <period ms>[m
[32m+[m[32mcode :[m
[32m+[m[32m  if (((#Clock).clock_hour >= <startHour>) and ((#Clock).clock_hour < <endHour>)) {[m
[32m+[m[32m    ...[m
[32m+[m[32m  } else {[m
[32m+[m[32m    break[m
[32m+[m[32m  }[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## [Example][m
[32m+[m[32m### Cron and period use case1: Run once now[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m{[m
[32m+[m[32m"cron": ""[m
[32m+[m[32m"period": -1[m
[32m+[m[32m"code: "action1, ..."[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m### Cron and period use case2: Run at 9 AM once[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m{[m
[32m+[m[32m"cron": "0 9 * * *"[m
[32m+[m[32m"period": -1[m
[32m+[m[32m"code": "action1, ..."[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m###  Daily 9 AM execution[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m{[m
[32m+[m[32m"cron": "0 9 * * *"[m
[32m+[m[32m"period": 0[m
[32m+[m[32m"code": "action1, ..."[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m###  Continuous 10-second monitoring[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m{[m
[32m+[m[32m"cron": ""[m
[32m+[m[32m"period": 10000[m
[32m+[m[32m"code": "action1, ..."[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Variable Management[m
[32m+[m[32m- all variables Declared with := after "name", "cron", and "period".[m
[32m+[m[32m- all variables Must be declared only inside the "code" block, do not place them inside or next to "period".[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Global variables[m
[32m+[m[32m- Global variables must be declared **strictly at the very beginning** of the "code" block, before any logic, if, or service (value or function) calls.[m
[32m+[m[32m- All variables must be declared once at the very beginning of the "code" block using :=, and **must be updated later using = during execution**.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Do not declare variables like curtainOpen := true in the middle of the "code" logic.[m
[32m+[m[32m- This ensures proper initialization and consistent scoping across executions.[m
[32m+[m[32mDeclared using :=, and persist across period executions within the same cron cycle.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Automatically reset on new cron trigger.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Reassigned with `=`**.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Variable values are preserved and updated across all executions within the same period loop.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Used for tracking global state across periods, such as counts, toggles, durations, triggers, and flags.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Local Variables[m
[32m+[m[32m- Declared within code blocks using `=`[m
[32m+[m[32m- Scoped to current period execution only[m
[32m+[m[32m### [Example][m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m{[m
[32m+[m[32m"cron": ""[m
[32m+[m[32m"period": 100[m
[32m+[m[32m"code":[m
[32m+[m[32m  status = (#Tag).value_service[m
[32m+[m[32m  if (status == value) {[m
[32m+[m[32m      // ... Execute code only at the moment the condition turns true[m
[32m+[m[32m  } else {[m
[32m+[m[32m    // Reset the flag when the condition is no longer true[m
[32m+[m[32m  }[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Device Control[m
[32m+[m[32m## Device Selection[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Every tag name is english**[m
[32m+[m[32m- Every receiver tag after `#` must start with an uppercase English letter.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Correct: `#Bedroom`, `#Sector1`, `#Entrance`, `#TemperatureSensor`[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Incorrect: `#bedroom`, `#sector1`, `#entrance`, `#temperaturesensor`[m
[32m+[m[32m- The tags can be combined from command.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Each device has pre-defined Tags (**device**, **location**, **group**...).[m
[32m+[m[32m- (#Tag1 #Tag2 ...) selects devices with ALL specified tags (AND logic, separated by spaces).[m
[32m+[m[32m- Access: `(#Tags).service_value` (read-only) or `(#Tags).service_function(args)` (control)[m
[32m+[m[32m- When using numeric comparisons or function arguments, follow the service descriptor units exactly. For example, if a voltage value has `return_descriptor` saying millivolts, compare `220V` as `220000`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Tags must be accurately **extracted from the command**, typically consisting of one device tag and a combination of user-defined tags like location, group, or multiple user-defined tags only.[m
[32m+[m[32m- A valid device selection typically consists of one device tag (e.g., #Light) and one or more user-defined tags such as #location, #group, etc.[m
[32m+[m[32m### [Example][m
[32m+[m[32mCommand: "Turn on the lights in the odd group"[m
[32m+[m[32m→ #Light is the device tag for "lights"[m
[32m+[m[32m→ #Odd is a user-defined group tag[m
[32m+[m[32m→ Combined expression: (#Light #Odd).switch_on()[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Additional Rule: When Tag is Not a Device Type[m
[32m+[m[32m[Step1] If the **tag** in the command is not found in the **device list** from **[service_list_value] or [service_list_function]** as a device tag:[m
[32m+[m[32m[Step2] Look up the tag in the [connected_devices] list.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Identify which devices contain the tag and extract their category (e.g., Light, Alarm).[m
[32m+[m[32m[Step3] - For each discovered category:[m
[32m+[m[32m- Check available control **function list** OR the **value list** for conditional checks and control actions[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m  (e.g., `switch_off()`, `alarm_off()`, `relativeHumidityMeasurement_humidity()`, etc.)[m
[32m+[m[32m[Step4] Generate all control commands per device type using the tag as a shared filter.[m
[32m+[m[32m**Note: Treat "모든 불을 꺼줘" and "불을 다 꺼줘" as equivalent. Both should be interpreted as requests to control all relevant devices, and represented using `all(#Light)` in the code. Do not distinguish between these phrasings.**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## !Rule: Device selection must always include valid device type tags[m
[32m+[m[32m- Any bracket-based selector like `(#...)`, `all(#...)`, `(#TagA #TagB)` must include **at least one valid device type**.[m
[32m+[m[32m- A **device type** is one explicitly defined in `service_list`, or resolvable via `connected_devices`.[m
[32m+[m[32m### Invalid Usage (must be avoided):[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m(#).switch_on()[m
[32m+[m[32mall().switch_on()[m
[32m+[m[32m().alarm_siren()[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m## !Rule: Reject tags not found in device list or connected devices[m
[32m+[m[32m- If a tag used in device selection (e.g., `(#Tag)`, `all(#Tag)`) is:[m
[32m+[m[32m  1. Not listed as a valid device type in `service_list`, **AND**[m
[32m+[m[32m  2. Cannot be resolved to a device category via `connected_devices`[m
[32m+[m[32m→ Then that tag is considered **invalid**, and **must not appear in any generated code**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### [Example1][m
[32m+[m[32m- Command: "Turn off all devices with tag Group1"[m
[32m+[m[32m- `#Group1` is not a device-type tag.[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m- From [connected_devices], we find:[m
[32m+[m[32m  {[m
[32m+[m[32m    "Group1_Light_Lower_Center": {[m
[32m+[m[32m      "category": "Light",[m
[32m+[m[32m      "tags": ["Group1", "Lower", "Center", "Light"][m
[32m+[m[32m    },[m
[32m+[m[32m    "Group1_Alarm_Upper_Left": {[m
[32m+[m[32m      "category": "Alarm",[m
[32m+[m[32m      "tags": ["Group1", "Upper", "Left", "Alarm"][m
[32m+[m[32m    }[m
[32m+[m[32m  }[m
[32m+[m[32m- Devices of category Light and Alarm both support switch_off() and alarm_off() respectively.[m
[32m+[m[32m- → Final JoILang code:[m
[32m+[m[32m  all(#Group1).switch_off()[m
[32m+[m[32m  all(#Group1).alarm_off()[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use this pattern to support generalized group operations when tag-only identifiers are used in the user's command:[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m{[m
[32m+[m[32m  "name": "Scenario1",[m
[32m+[m[32m  "cron": "",[m
[32m+[m[32m  "period": -1,[m
[32m+[m[32m  "code": "all(#Group1).switch_off()\nall(#Group1).alarm_off()"[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m### [Example2][m
[32m+[m[32m  - Command: "하우스A 모두 닫아줘."[m
[32m+[m[32m  [Step1] **Tag** SectorA can not searched in **device list**.[m
[32m+[m[32m  [Step2] with SectorA, it can find blind device in the [connected_devices] list.[m
[32m+[m[32m  [Step3] And blind device has blind_close function.[m
[32m+[m[32m  "s_blind_1": {[m
[32m+[m[32m    "category": "Blind",[m
[32m+[m[32m    "tags": ["SectorA", "odd", "Blind"][m
[32m+[m[32m  },[m
[32m+[m[32m  [Step4] Finally,[m
[32m+[m[32m  ```[m
[32m+[m[32m  {"name": "Scenario1", "cron": "", "period": -1, "code": "all(#SectorA).blind_close()"}[m
[32m+[m[32m  ```[m
[32m+[m[32m### [Example3][m
[32m+[m[32m  - Command: "If any Group2 exceeds 80, turn off Group2"[m
[32m+[m[32m  [Step1] #Group2 is not found in the device list[m
[32m+[m[32m  [Step2] From [connected_devices] we find:[m
[32m+[m[32m  {"Group2_HumiditySensor_Upper_Left": {[m
[32m+[m[32m    "category": "HumiditySensor",[m
[32m+[m[32m    "tags": ["Group2", "Upper", "Left", "HumiditySensor"][m
[32m+[m[32m  }}[m
[32m+[m[32m  [Step3] From the service [value, function] list, we find that HumiditySensor provides relativeHumidityMeasurement_humidity[m
[32m+[m[32m  [Step4] → Final JoILang Code:[m
[32m+[m[32m  ```[m
[32m+[m[32m  {[m
[32m+[m[32m  "name": "<Set the "name" field using a **brief and intuitive summary** of the command's intent.>",[m
[32m+[m[32m  "cron": "",[m
[32m+[m[32m  "period": -1,[m
[32m+[m[32m  "code": "if(any(#Group2).relativeHumidityMeasurement_humidity > 80) {\n[m
[32m+[m[32m    (#Group2).switch_off()\n}"[m
[32m+[m[32m  }[m
[32m+[m[32m  ```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Collective Operations[m
[32m+[m[32mUse `all(...)` or `any(...)` **only if** explicitly requested for all/any devices.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `(#Tag).function()`: Apply function to some of matching devices(default)[m
[32m+[m[32m- `all(#Tag).function()`: Apply function to ALL matching devices[m
[32m+[m[32m- `all(#Tag).attribute == value`: True if ALL devices match condition[m
[32m+[m[32m- `any(#Tag).attribute == value`: True if ANY device matches condition[m
[32m+[m[32m- If any temperature sensor in sector A reads above 30 degrees, turn on all fans.[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mif (any(#SectorA).temperaturesensor_temperature > 30.0) {[m
[32m+[m[32m  all(#Fan).switch_on()[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Control Flow[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Condition Logic[m
[32m+[m[32m- `if (cond) { }`, `if (cond) { } else { }`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `if ((condA) and (condB))`, `if ((condA) or (condB))`[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use explicit boolean comparisons for conditions (e.g., `attribute == true`).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Loop Control[m
[32m+[m[32m- **No `for` loops allowed**[m
[32m+[m[32m- **No `while` loops allowed**[m
[32m+[m[32m- All repetition controlled via `cron` and `period`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `break`: Stops current/future periods until next cron.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - With cron = "": stops permanently after break[m
[32m+[m[32m  - With scheduled cron: stops until next cron trigger[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Blocking Operations[m
[32m+[m[32m- `wait until(condition)`: Pauses the execution of all subsequent statements in the current period until the specified condition becomes true. Once the condition is satisfied, the next lines are executed sequentially. While waiting, no other commands run, even if the period interval elapses. New triggers within the same cron cycle are ignored during this wait.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `delay(N SEC|MIN|HOUR)`: Delays execution for the specified duration, then continues with the next statement. Use this helper for between-action waits in dataset JOICode. It must be a standalone statement and must not be used with `wait until` or passed as an argument.[m
[32m+[m[32m- This enables event-driven behavior in periodic scenarios (period >= 100).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Expression Rules[m
[32m+[m[32m### Arithmetic Operations[m
[32m+[m[32m- Operators: `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `=`[m
[32m+[m[32m- Must assign to variable before using in methods (value/function) calls[m
[32m+[m[32m- String concatenation is not allowed. No Template Literals. Only static strings or single variable messages are allowed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Service Value & Function Arguments Best Practice[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Whenever you use a service_value as a function argument, assign it to a variable first and then pass the variable as the argument.[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m  (Do not pass service_value expressions directly in function calls.)[m
[32m+[m[32m- A service_value access must never be followed by another method call using dot chaining.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Incorrect:[m
[32m+[m[32m    `(#HumiditySensor).humiditysensor_humidity.speaker_speak(string(humiditysensor_humidity))`[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Correct:[m
[32m+[m[32m    `hum = (#HumiditySensor).humiditysensor_humidity`[m
[32m+[m[32m    `(#Speaker).speaker_speak(hum)`[m
[32m+[m[32m- If a variable is created from a service_value, that variable must be consumed later.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Incorrect:[m
[32m+[m[32m    `power = (#Charger).charger_power`[m
[32m+[m[32m    `(#Speaker).speaker_speak("Power consumption is ")`[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Correct:[m
[32m+[m[32m    `power = (#Charger).charger_power`[m
[32m+[m[32m    `(#Speaker).speaker_speak(power)`[m
[32m+[m[32m- For simple numbers or text, you can use literals directly, or assign to a variable first if desired.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Example:[m
[32m+[m[32m    ```[m
[32m+[m[32m    temp = (#TemperatureSensor).temperaturesensor_temperature[m
[32m+[m[32m    (#AirConditioner).airconditioner_settargettemperature(temp)[m
[32m+[m[32m    (#Speaker).speaker_speak("Hello")[m
[32m+[m[32m    ```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### [Example][m
[32m+[m[32m#### Valid Case:[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mtemp = (#TemperatureSensor).temperaturesensor_temperature[m
[32m+[m[32madjusted = temp - 5[m
[32m+[m[32m(#AirConditioner).airconditioner_settargettemperature(adjusted)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m#### Invalid Case:[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mtemperature = (#TemperatureSensor).temperaturesensor_temperature + 5[m
[32m+[m[32m(#AirConditioner).airconditioner_settargettemperature( temperature )[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Boolean Operations[m
[32m+[m[32m- Comparisons: `==`, `!=`, `>`, `<`, `>=`, `<=`[m
[32m+[m[32m- Logic: `and`, `or`[m
[32m+[m[32m- All conditions must evaluate to explicit boolean values[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### [Example][m
[32m+[m[32m#### Valid Case:[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mif ((#Tag).booleanService == true) {[m
[32m+[m[32m  // do something[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32mif ((#Tag).integerService > 25) {[m
[32m+[m[32m    // do something[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m#### Invalid Case:[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mif ((#Tag).booleanService) {[m
[32m+[m[32m  action, ...[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Error Handling & Communication[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### User Feedback[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use `(#Speaker).speaker_speak("message")` to explain issues[m
[32m+[m[32m- Handle missing or unsupported devices gracefully[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Device Alternatives[m
[32m+[m[32m- Multiple devices may provide same functionality:[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Alerts: `(#Alarm).alarm_siren()` or `(#Siren).siren_setsirenmode('siren')`[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Presence: `(#PresenceSensor).presencesensor_presence` or an equivalent current presence service from the injected schema[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Best Practices[m
[32m+[m[32m- Declare `name`, `cron`, `period` first.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Initialize global variables immediately after period.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use explicit boolean comparisons.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Assign arithmetic results to variables before method (service/function) calls[m
[32m+[m[32m- **DO NOT** use `for` or `while` loops.[m
[32m+[m[32m</GRAMMAR>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## FORMAT[m
[32m+[m[32m### Input[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mCurrent Time: "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS"[m
[32m+[m[32mGenerate JOI Lang code for: <user_command>[m
[32m+[m[32m[Additional context: <optional_info>][m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Output[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mname = "Scenario1"[m
[32m+[m[32mcron = <cron_expression>[m
[32m+[m[32mperiod = <integer>[m
[32m+[m[32mcode =[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m[global_var := <initial_value>][m
[32m+[m[32m[local_var = <changed_value_for_each_period>][m
[32m+[m[32m<code_block>[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mKey Rules:[m
[32m+[m[32m- Each scenario executes independently and concurrently.[m
[32m+[m[32m- No data sharing between scenarios.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Generation Guidelines[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Language Interpretation[m
[32m+[m[32m- Follow user commands literally and precisely, avoiding over-interpretation.[m
[32m+[m[32m- "When A happens": Use `wait until` (state change/suspension).[m
[32m+[m[32m- "If A is true": Use `if/else` (single-time condition check).[m
[32m+[m[32m- "Every": Use appropriate `cron` and `period` settings.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m[32m[Condition Combination Rules][m
[32m+[m[32m### 1. Static condition (state check): ~였으면, ~인 상태면, ~라면 (If)[m
[32m+[m[32m   - This applies when the condition is already true at the time of evaluation.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - The system simply checks the current state and executes immediately if the condition is met.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - It assumes that the state has already been sustained for some time.[m
[32m+[m[32m   Common Expressions:[m
[32m+[m[32m      "if it is...", "if the state is...", "in case of..."[m
[32m+[m[32m   #### Caution:[m
[32m+[m[32m   - if (...) only checks the current state.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - It does not detect or care about any prior changes.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - It will not trigger if the system is waiting for a transition (e.g., from "off" to "on").[m
[32m+[m[32m   **Applies when the state is already true at evaluation time.**[m
[32m+[m[32m   #### [example][m
[32m+[m[32m   - “if the door is closed” → if ((#Door).doorControl_door == "closed")[m
[32m+[m[32m   - “if the light is on” → if ((#Light).switch_switch == "on")[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Korean command: “문이 닫혀 있으면”[m
[32m+[m[32m   - English translated command: "if the door is closed"[m
[32m+[m[32m   - → if ((#Door).doorControl_door == "closed")[m
[32m+[m[32m   - 현재 상태가 닫힘일 때 즉시 실행[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 2. Dynamic transition (state change detection): ~하면, ~되면, ~하게 되면 (When)[m
[32m+[m[32m   **Triggers only when the condition becomes true from the opposite state.**[m
[32m+[m[32m   **If the condition implies a **transition** from a previous numeric state (e.g., below threshold → above threshold)**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - This triggers only when a condition changes from false to true.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - It captures a moment of change, not just a static state.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - This is important for event-driven scenarios where the system must wait for a state to become true.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - **Important**: Even though this looks like a numeric threshold, it still implies a **change in state** (from <80 to >=80), and must be treated as **Dynamic Transition**.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - And uses words like “되면”, “넘으면”, “이상이 되면”, “떨어지면”,[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Then use:[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   → `wait until (...)`[m
[32m+[m[32m   #### [incorrect][m
[32m+[m[32m   - DO NOT use `if (humidity >= 80)` for:[m
[32m+[m[32m   - "습도가 80% 이상이 되면"[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   - Instead, use `wait until (humidity >= 80)`[m
[32m+[m[32m   #### [example2][m
[32m+[m[32m   - “습도가 80% 이상이 되면 블라인드를 내려 줘.”[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   → `wait until ((#HumiditySensor).relativeHumidityMeasurement_humidity >= 80.0)`[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   → `(#Blind).windowShade_close()`[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Korean command: "습도가 80% 이상이 되면"[m
[32m+[m[32m   - English translated command: "when humidity becomes greater than or equal to 80%"[m
[32m+[m[32m   - → `wait until((#HumiditySensor).relativeHumidityMeasurement_humidity >= 80.0)`[m
[32m+[m[32m   - DO NOT use `if (...)` for threshold-based transitions unless the command explicitly implies the condition is already true at evaluation time.[m
[32m+[m[32m   #### [example2][m
[32m+[m[32m   - Korean command: “문이 닫히면”[m
[32m+[m[32m   - English translated command: "when the door closes"[m
[32m+[m[32m   - → wait until ((#Door).doorControl_door == "closed"),[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m   - Korean command: "제습기가 꺼지면"[m
[32m+[m[32m   - → wait until((#Dehumidifier).switch_switch == "off")[m
[32m+[m[32m   **Also used for one-time triggering events** in below **4. One-Time Trigger + Repeating Action** patterns.[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   - For example, in:[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   > "When the door closes, then every 5 seconds do X"[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   The phrase "when the door closes" is classified as a **Dynamic transition** - a one-time trigger that leads to a repeating action loop.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Therefore, **Step 4 should treat any such one-time event detection via `wait until (...)` as a [2] Dynamic transition**, regardless of what follows.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 3-1. [Combined condition]: ~였다가 ~하면, ~였거나 ~하면, ~이거나 ~하면 (If + when, If + And then)[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Korean command: "비어있다가 누군가 감지되면"[m
[32m+[m[32m   - "**비어있다가**" is **state check(과거 상태 검사)** + "누군가 감지되면" **state change(미래 변화 감지)**를 모두 수용[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Korean command: “문이 닫혀있거나 닫히면”[m
[32m+[m[32m   - English translated command: "if or when the door is closed"[m
[32m+[m[32m   - → if ((#Door).doorControl_door == "closed") { ... } else { wait until ((#Door).doorControl_door == "closed") }[m
[32m+[m[32m   - 현재 상태가 이미 참인지 확인하고, 아니라면 그 상태가 미래에 될 때까지 기다리는 방식[m
[32m+[m[32m   - 즉, **state check(현재 상태 검사)**와 **state change(미래 변화 감지)**를 모두 수용[m
[32m+[m[32m   - 이 두 조건은 시간상 연속되지 않아도 되며, 서로 독립적으로 만족될 수 있음[m
[32m+[m[32m   #### [Example]: “토양 습도가 20% 이상인데 알람이 켜지게 되면 물을 줘” → 토양 상태와 알람 이벤트는 독립적이며, 둘 다 충족되었을 때 실행[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Use: if (토양 습도 state check) { wait until (알람 state change) }[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Reacts to either current satisfaction or future transition—whichever happens—ensuring coverage of both temporal paths.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 3-2. [Combined condition]: = ~하고 ~하면, (When + When)[m[41m   [m
[32m+[m[32m   - Separately,When a condition involves **two consecutive state changes**, like “A happened, and then B happens”[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m   - Korean command: "**비었다가** 누군가 감지되면"[m
[32m+[m[32m   - "**비었다가**" is **state check(현재 변화 감지)** + "누군가 감지되면" **state change(미래 변화 감지)**를 모두 수용[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Korean example: “문이 닫혔다 열리면”, “비가 오는데 창문이 열려 있으면”[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   - → Use **two `wait until` statements** to capture both transitions when events must occur in sequence.[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   - If the condition requires simultaneous truth (e.g., “if it's raining and the window is open”), use a single `if (...) and (...)` block instead.[m
[32m+[m[32m   #### [Example] "문이 열렸다 닫히면 알림을 울려줘."[m
[32m+[m[32m   ```[m
[32m+[m[32m   {"name": "DoorClosedAlert", "cron": "", "period": -1, "code":[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m   "wait until((#DoorLock).doorControl_door == \"open\")\n[m
[32m+[m[32m   wait until((#DoorLock).doorControl_door == \"closed\")\n(#Alarm).alarm_siren()"}[m
[32m+[m[32m   ```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 4. [One-Time Trigger (Dynamic transition) + Subsequent Repeating Action][m
[32m+[m[32m- When the natural language includes phrases like “after ~, repeat every N seconds”,[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32mit should be interpreted as a **one-time condition trigger** is Dynamic transition. and, followed by a **periodic loop** of actions.[m
[32m+[m[32m#### Key Principles[m
[32m+[m[32m- Detect the **triggering event** only once using **Dynamic transition (state change detection)** `wait until (...)` or **Static condition (state check)** `if`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Control repeated actions using `period > 0` and a Boolean flag variable.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use flags like `triggered := false` or `action := false` to maintain state inside the loop.[m
[32m+[m[32m#### [Example][m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m**Command**:[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m- "When the front door closes, immediately turn off the light, and then flash the strobe every 3 seconds."[m
[32m+[m[32m**Interpretation**:[m
[32m+[m[32m- `"when the door closes"` → single detection via `wait until (...)`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `"every 3 seconds"` → continuous action with `period: 3000`[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m{[m
[32m+[m[32m  "name": "Scenario1",[m
[32m+[m[32m  "cron": "",[m
[32m+[m[32m  "period": 3000,[m
[32m+[m[32m  "code": "[m
[32m+[m[32m   action := false\n[m
[32m+[m[32m   if (action == false) {\n[m
[32m+[m[32m      wait until ((#Door).doorControl_door == \"closed\")\n[m
[32m+[m[32m      (#Light).switch_off()\n[m
[32m+[m[32m      action = true\n[m
[32m+[m[32m   }\n[m
[32m+[m[32m   else {\n[m
[32m+[m[32m      (#Alarm).alarm_strobe()\n[m
[32m+[m[32m   }"[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 5. [Combined condition + Repeating condition] (dynamic + periodic): ~할 때마다, ~하게 될 때마다 + 주기적으로 ~해줘 (loop는 period를 의미).[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Korean command: “문이 열릴 때마다”[m
[32m+[m[32m   - English translated command: "whenever the door opens"[m
[32m+[m[32m   - → use with period > 0 loop:[m
[32m+[m[32m     if ((#Door).doorControl_door == "closed") { wait until ((#Door).doorControl_door == "open") }[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Korean command: “문이 열릴 때마다”, “문이 닫혔다 열릴 때마다 사진을 5초 단위로 찍어줘”[m
[32m+[m[32m   - English translated command: "whenever the door opens", "after the door closes and opens, take a photo every 5 seconds"[m
[32m+[m[32m   - **If the sentence explicitly mentions a specific repeating interval (such as "every 5 seconds", "5초마다"), always convert this interval to milliseconds and set it as the period value (e.g., period = 5000 for 5 seconds).**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - **If the sentence describes a repeating, continuous, or monitoring action but does not mention a specific interval, or obviously requires a period but no interval is stated, always set the period to 100 (ms) by default.**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - → Use with "period": 100 to continuously monitor state transitions and respond in real time.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - → Combine state change detection with `period` and state variables. For a between-action wait, use `delay(N SEC|MIN|HOUR)`.[m
[32m+[m[32m   [example][m
[32m+[m[32m   ```[m
[32m+[m[32m   "name": "Scenario",[m
[32m+[m[32m   "cron": "",[m
[32m+[m[32m   "period": 5000,[m
[32m+[m[32m   "code": "[m
[32m+[m[32m      phase := false\n[m
[32m+[m[32m      if (phase == false) {\n[m
[32m+[m[32m         wait until((#DoorLock).doorControl_door == 'closed')\n[m
[32m+[m[32m         wait until((#DoorLock).doorControl_door == 'open')\n[m
[32m+[m[32m         phase = true\n[m
[32m+[m[32m      } else {\n[m
[32m+[m[32m         (#Camera).camera_take()\n[m
[32m+[m[32m      }[m
[32m+[m[32m   "[m
[32m+[m[32m   ```[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Use this pattern when a condition leads to continuous behavior (e.g., taking photos every N seconds) rather than a one-time reaction.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - When a command includes both a **"state-based trigger" (~할 때마다)** and a **"fixed time loop" (e.g., every 2 seconds)**, you **must use `period` with a state flag variable** to prevent repeated triggering within the same state.[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   - This ensures actions occur **only once per transition** while still checking repeatedly.[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   - You must initialize a **boolean variable** using `:=` and reset it appropriately to track state transitions accurately.[m
[32m+[m[32m   #### [Example][m
[32m+[m[32m   **Korean:** `2초마다 상태를 확인해서 TV가 켜질 때마다 스피커도 켜 줘.`[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   **JoILang:**[m
[32m+[m[32m   ```[m
[32m+[m[32m      "name": "Scenario1",[m
[32m+[m[32m      "cron": "",[m
[32m+[m[32m      "period": 2000,[m
[32m+[m[32m      "code": "[m
[32m+[m[32m      triggered := false[m
[32m+[m[32m      if ((#Television).switch_switch == "on") {[m
[32m+[m[32m         if (triggered == false) {[m
[32m+[m[32m         (#Speaker).switch_on()[m
[32m+[m[32m         triggered = true[m
[32m+[m[32m         }[m
[32m+[m[32m         } else {[m
[32m+[m[32m         triggered = false[m
[32m+[m[32m      }[m
[32m+[m[32m   ```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 6. [Periodic Monitoring / Repeating Execution]: 실시간으로 ~할 때마다, 계속 ~하면 ~해줘, ~동안 ~하면 ~해줘[m
[32m+[m[32m   - These expressions describe conditions that must be repeatedly checked over time.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Common phrases include:[m
[32m+[m[32m   - "실시간으로 ~할 때마다"[m
[32m+[m[32m   - "계속 ~하면"[m
[32m+[m[32m   - "계속 확인해서 ~할 때마다"[m
[32m+[m[32m   - "~동안 ~하면"[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   #### 🧠 Key Principle:[m
[32m+[m[32m   - If **no explicit interval** is provided (e.g., “매 5초마다”), then **"실시간", "계속" 등 표현이 있을 경우 `period: 100`이 기본값(default)**으로 적용되어야 합니다.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - This ensures that the system **monitors state changes frequently and promptly**, as expected from real-time behavior.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   #### ✅ Correct Default:[m
[32m+[m[32m   - `"실시간으로 확인하여 ~할 때마다"` → `period: 100`[m
[32m+[m[32m   - `"계속 확인해서 ~할 때마다"` → `period: 100`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   #### ❌ Incorrect (Do NOT use by default):[m
[32m+[m[32m   - `"실시간"인데 period: 10000` → too slow; not real-time.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   ---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   ### ⚠️ 문맥 구분 가이드:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   #### 1️⃣ “실시간으로 확인하여 **현재 상태가 참일 때마다** 행동”[m
[32m+[m[32m   - → 현재 상태를 주기적으로 검사하고, 조건이 참이면 실행[m
[32m+[m[32m   - → `if ((#Sensor).sensor_value == "on") { ... }`[m
[32m+[m[32m   - → 반복 실행 필요 → `period: 100`[m
[32m+[m[32m   - ✅ 상태 유지 기반 루프[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   #### 2️⃣ “실시간으로 확인하여 **변화가 발생할 때마다** (ex. '되다', '변하다')”[m
[32m+[m[32m   - → 이전과 다른 상태로 바뀔 때마다 반응[m
[32m+[m[32m   - → 상태 전이 감지를 위한 flag 필요[m
[32m+[m[32m   - ✅ JoILang에서는 `triggered := false` 등 Boolean flag로 transition 감지[m
[32m+[m[32m   - ✅ 역시 `period: 100` 필요[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   #### [예시 1][m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   **Command**:[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   > 실시간으로 확인하여 재실 센서가 감지 상태일 때마다 10초 대기 후 조명의 밝기를 현재 밝기로 맞춰줘.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   - 반복 체크 → `period: 100`[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   - 조건이 항상 true일 수 있으므로 flag 필요[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   - → 상태 유지 기반[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   #### [예시 2][m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   **Command**:[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   > 실시간으로 확인하여 재실 센서가 감지 상태가 될 때마다 조명을 켜줘.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   - 상태 변화 → `off → on` 전이 탐지[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   - → `triggered := false` 등 flag 사용[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m   - → `period: 100`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   ```json[m
[32m+[m[32m   {[m
[32m+[m[32m   "name": "PresenceTrigger",[m
[32m+[m[32m   "cron": "",[m
[32m+[m[32m   "period": 100,[m
[32m+[m[32m   "code": "[m
[32m+[m[32m      triggered := false[m
[32m+[m[32m      if ((#Presence).presenceSensor_presence == \"present\") {[m
[32m+[m[32m         if (triggered == false) {[m
[32m+[m[32m         (#Light).switch_on()[m
[32m+[m[32m         triggered = true[m
[32m+[m[32m         }[m
[32m+[m[32m      } else {[m
[32m+[m[32m         triggered = false[m
[32m+[m[32m      }[m
[32m+[m[32m   "[m
[32m+[m[32m   }[m
[32m+[m[32m   ```[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Requires periodic check or loop (period) to react to each occurrence.[m
