[32m+[m[32m### Avoid Separating into Multiple Scenarios When Using "Then", "After That"[m
[32m+[m[32m- When a sentence ends with an action followed by a phrase like **"then do X"** or **"after that, do Y"**, try to **keep the scenario unified** instead of breaking it into multiple blocks with `wait until` across different steps or scenarios.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use `wait until` **within** the same script block if needed, to maintain continuity.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Important: The wait until statement must only contain condition expressions, not action calls.[m
[32m+[m[32m- You must not write: wait until ((#Clock).clock_delay(5000))[m
[32m+[m[32m- Instead, if a between-action delay is intended, use `delay(5 SEC)` as a standalone statement, not inside wait until.[m
[32m+[m[32m#### [Example][m
[32m+[m[32m**Korean Natural Command:**[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m> 매일 오전 7시에 관개 장치가 꺼져 있고 창문이 닫혀 있으면 관개 장치를 켜고 창문을 열어 줘. 이후 관개 장치가 켜지면 블라인드를 닫아 줘.[m
[32m+[m[32m**JoILang Code:**[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m{[m
[32m+[m[32m  "name": "Scenario1",[m
[32m+[m[32m  "cron": "0 7 * * *",[m
[32m+[m[32m  "period": -1,[m
[32m+[m[32m  "code": "if ((#Irrigator).switch_switch == \"off\" and (#WindowCovering).windowcovering_currentposition == 0) {\n  (#Irrigator).switch_on()\n  (#WindowCovering).windowcovering_uporopen()\n  wait until ((#Irrigator).switch_switch == \"on\")\n  (#WindowCovering).windowcovering_downorclose()\n}"[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
