[32m+[m[32m## Error Handling & Communication[m
[32m+[m[32m### User Feedback[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use `(#Speaker).speaker_speak("message")` to explain issues[m
[32m+[m[32m- Handle missing or unsupported devices gracefully[m
[32m+[m[32m### Best Practices[m
[32m+[m[32m- Declare `name`, `cron`, `period` first.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Initialize global variables immediately after period.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use explicit boolean comparisons.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Assign arithmetic results to variables before method calls[m
[32m+[m[32m- **DO NOT** use `for` or `while` loops.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## [**contacts**] Handling Contact Information for Personalized Actions[m
[32m+[m[32m- When `contacts` (a list of person records) is provided via `other_params`, extract the relevant recipient information (name, email, birthday, etc.) based on the user's instruction.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The contact entry for the current user (`"me"`) must be recognized and **excluded** from mass communication unless explicitly included.[m
[32m+[m[32m- For birthday-related scenarios:[m
[32m+[m[32m  - If the instruction is to **notify others** about the speaker’s own birthday:[m
[32m+[m[32m    - Identify the current user’s birthday using the `"me"` record.[m
[32m+[m[32m    - Send emails to **all other contacts** (i.e., those not named `"me"`), using the subject and content described in the command.[m
[32m+[m[32m    - Example pattern:[m
[32m+[m[32m      ```plaintext[m
[32m+[m[32m      "Send everyone except me an email titled 'Birthday Reminder' with the content 'My birthday is YYYY-MM-DD'."[m
[32m+[m[32m      ```[m
[32m+[m[32m- When referencing specific individuals (e.g., by name), search the `contacts` list and extract `email` or `contact` fields to execute relevant functions (e.g., email, call).[m
[32m+[m[32m- In case of missing target emails or names not matched in `contacts`, optionally use `(#Speaker).speaker_speak("Cannot find contact for [name]")` to inform the user.[m
[32m+[m[32m- All actions must be resolved to explicit device commands such as:[m
[32m+[m[32m  (#EmailProvider).emailProvider_sendMail(email, subject, content)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## When an action depends on a previous condition or event with repeat[m
[32m+[m[32m- **after the light turns on, repeat...**, try to express the entire flow as a single scenario use **global variable**[m
[32m+[m[32m- All global variables must be declared with the `:=` operator at the very start of the `code:` section, before any other statements.[m
[32m+[m[32m- always express the entire flow as a single scenario, and instead of checking device states directly with wait until ((#Device).state == "value"),[m
[32m+[m[32muse a global variable (e.g., triggered := false) declared at the top of the "code" block and write wait until (triggered == true) to represent the dependency.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use `delay(N SEC|MIN|HOUR)` for between-action waits. Avoid delays if the behavior is intended to occur only once without ongoing repetition.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Cron and Period timing[m
[32m+[m[32m- Period: -1[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Execute once, then stop scenario.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Period: 0[m
[32m+[m[32m  - **Repeat** every cron timing[m
[32m+[m[32m  - **Daily**, **Every** Case[m[41m [m
[32m+[m[32m  - Execute once **per cron** trigger. (no further execution within the same cron cycle)[m
[32m+[m[32m- `>= 100`: Repeat every period milliseconds (continuous monitoring).[m
