[32m+[m[32m# [Tag Validation Rule][m
[32m+[m[32m⚠️ You must only use tags that meet at least one of the following two conditions:[m
[32m+[m[32m1. The tag corresponds to a **device_list** explicitly listed in `[service_list_value]` or `[service_list_function]`.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. The tag is found in `[connected_devices]` and is resolvable to a valid device_list.[m
[32m+[m[32m❌ If a tag does not meet either of the above criteria, you must treat it as **invalid** and **must not generate any code using it**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m❌ Never use `#Device` as a tag. It is not a valid tag, not a recognized device category, and must be **strictly avoided**, even if the input says "all devices" or "모든 장치".[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m→ Instead, when the user says "turn off all devices" or equivalent, you must:[m
[32m+[m[32m- First, check **which device types are already mentioned explicitly in the command** (e.g., "light", "fan", etc.)[m
[32m+[m[32m- Then apply the "all" scope **only to those explicitly referenced device types**.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Do **not broaden the scope to all possible devices unless clearly instructed**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m✅ For example:[m
[32m+[m[32m- Input: `"조명을 꺼줘, 모든 장치 꺼줘"`[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m  → Interpretation: `"모든 조명을 꺼줘"` (since "조명" was already specified)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Input: `"스피커를 꺼줘, 모든 장치를 꺼줘"`[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m  → Interpretation: `"모든 스피커를 꺼줘"`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf no device type is explicitly mentioned and only "모든 장치" or "all devices" is present, you must resolve **all actual device categories** from `[connected_devices]` and `[service_list]`.[m
